980
00:50:12.471 --> 00:50:13.472
I'd love to get involved.

981
00:50:13.555 --> 00:50:16.058
Hey. man. I'm always open to
a new business opportunity.

982
00:50:16.141 --> 00:50:18.393
Oh. I know it. Go check out my bathrooms.

983
00:50:18.477 --> 00:50:20.854
I got 15 toilets in this place.
and they're all your Luxos MTs.

984
00:50:20.938 --> 00:50:23.106
- Stop it. [laughing]
- Every one of them.

985
00:50:23.190 --> 00:50:24.942
Hey. a man after my own heart.

986
00:50:25.025 --> 00:50:27.861
[stammers] That's great timing
actually because. uh. nature's calling.

987
00:50:27.945 --> 00:50:28.946
[Ashe] Oh. Ooh. ooh.

988
00:50:29.029 --> 00:50:30.030
To more strong-ass gyms.

989
00:50:30.113 --> 00:50:31.532
To more. Many more. More than two.

990
00:50:31.615 --> 00:50:33.450
- Come on. come on. Go big.
- [Nick] Yeah.

991
00:50:33.534 --> 00:50:35.577
- [chuckles] I'm going big.
- [chuckles]

992
00:50:36.328 --> 00:50:37.871
- We haven't officially met.
- Hey.

993
00:50:37.955 --> 00:50:40.123
Barney Choi. I manage Nick's money.

994
00:50:40.207 --> 00:50:43.877
as well as a handful
of other high net worth people out here.

995
00:50:43.961 --> 00:50:46.004
Happy to help with
anything you might need.

996
00:50:46.088 --> 00:50:48.966
Hey. great. Always one-stop shopping
around here. I love it.

997
00:50:49.049 --> 00:50:50.050
- Barney. is it?
- Mm-hmm.

998
00:50:50.133 --> 00:50:51.885
Yeah. well. give me a little time
to get my bearings.

999
00:50:51.969 --> 00:50:53.262
and you and I should have dinner.

1000
00:50:53.345 --> 00:50:54.847
I've been looking for
some new opportunities.

1001
00:50:54.930 --> 00:50:56.473
- I'm your man.
- Great.

1002
00:51:00.435 --> 00:51:02.479
- [guests cheering]
- [energetic song on violin]

1003
00:51:13.740 --> 00:51:15.993
[cheering continues]

1004
00:51:53.530 --> 00:51:55.240
[DJ] ♪ Go ahead
Go ahead ♪

1005
00:51:55.324 --> 00:51:56.992
♪ Go ahead
Go rock back ♪

1006
00:51:57.075 --> 00:51:58.535
♪ Get that
Go ahead ♪

1007
00:51:58.619 --> 00:52:00.537
♪ Go ahead. now
Baby. go ahead ♪

1008
00:52:00.621 --> 00:52:02.331
♪ You got it
You got it ♪

1009
00:52:02.414 --> 00:52:04.082
♪ Go ahead
That's it ♪

1010
00:52:04.166 --> 00:52:05.250
♪ You got it
Go ahead ♪

1011
00:52:05.334 --> 00:52:07.044
[mix playing]

1012
00:52:09.296 --> 00:52:11.089
♪ Go ahead
Go ahead ♪

1013
00:52:12.132 --> 00:52:14.760
♪ Right
Gotta dance with her ass out ♪

1014
00:52:14.843 --> 00:52:16.178
♪ From the front to the back. now ♪

1015
00:52:16.678 --> 00:52:18.305
♪ From the side to the side. now ♪

1016
00:52:18.388 --> 00:52:19.765
♪ To the other side
Rock now ♪

1017
00:52:20.307 --> 00:52:21.350
♪ Out of breath
Real quick now ♪

1018
00:52:21.433 --> 00:52:23.227
[mix playing]

1019
00:52:31.777 --> 00:52:34.029
[music continues]

1020
00:52:42.829 --> 00:52:45.249
[laughs]

1021
00:52:45.332 --> 00:52:46.750
Hey. Where's Lisa tonight?

1022
00:52:46.834 --> 00:52:51.421
Oh. you know. she's. uh.
taking selfies in Milan. or Paris. or…

1023
00:52:51.505 --> 00:52:53.006
- [mutters]
- Still?

1024
00:52:53.674 --> 00:52:57.177
Yeah. Turns out fashion week
is not actually a week.

1025
00:52:57.261 --> 00:53:00.055
Hey. sweetheart.
can you please get me another cocktail?

1026
00:53:00.138 --> 00:53:01.807
Or maybe it's time we called it a night.

1027
00:53:02.516 --> 00:53:04.226
Gordy. you get me another drink.

1028
00:53:04.309 --> 00:53:06.395
[Gordy] Oh. I'm not getting involved.

1029
00:53:06.478 --> 00:53:08.313
Fine. I will get it myself.

1030
00:53:08.397 --> 00:53:09.565
[stammers] Diane. come on.

1031
00:53:09.648 --> 00:53:11.358
- [Diane] Okay. No. No!
- Let's get you home.

1032
00:53:11.441 --> 00:53:13.443
- [screams]
- [Peter] Diane--

1033
00:53:14.319 --> 00:53:17.322
[guests murmuring]

1034
00:53:21.368 --> 00:53:23.537
[panting]

1035
00:53:26.874 --> 00:53:27.958
[chuckles]

1036
00:53:31.587 --> 00:53:33.547
There comes a moment at every soiree

1037
00:53:33.630 --> 00:53:37.676
when it falls upon the host
to decide if the night has ended…

1038
00:53:41.471 --> 00:53:43.807
or if it's just beginning.

1039
00:53:44.725 --> 00:53:46.810
- [shouts]
- [guests clamoring]

1040
00:53:47.769 --> 00:53:49.855
[guests cheering]

1041
00:53:50.939 --> 00:53:51.940
Everybody in!

1042
00:53:52.983 --> 00:53:54.109
Yeah!

1043
00:53:57.905 --> 00:53:59.448
Turn up the music!

1044
00:54:03.619 --> 00:54:05.370
[cheering continues]

1045
00:54:08.582 --> 00:54:10.083
What is going on?

1046
00:54:12.211 --> 00:54:13.587
Thought we were fighting.

1047
00:54:14.713 --> 00:54:15.923
We're not fighting.

1048
00:54:20.260 --> 00:54:21.637
But if we were fighting. you would…

1049
00:54:21.720 --> 00:54:23.555
- No. Coop. No. Coop.
- …you would lose.

1050
00:54:23.639 --> 00:54:24.681
- No! No!
- [laughs] Yes.

1051
00:54:24.765 --> 00:54:27.184
- Coop. you're gonna-- [screams]
- Bye.

1052
00:54:30.145 --> 00:54:31.730
[exclaiming]

1053
00:54:34.191 --> 00:54:37.027
[guests shout. cheer]

1054
00:54:37.110 --> 00:54:38.820
[party music continues]

1055
00:54:45.702 --> 00:54:48.288
[cheering continues]

1056
00:54:56.171 --> 00:54:58.465
[house music playing in distance]

1057
00:54:59.925 --> 00:55:01.301
You've been avoiding me.

1058
00:55:04.012 --> 00:55:05.097
It was a lot to process.

1059
00:55:05.180 --> 00:55:07.015
[chuckles] Yeah.

1060
00:55:12.020 --> 00:55:14.147
Why didn't you take
your job at Bailey back?

1061
00:55:17.401 --> 00:55:18.902
The truth is. I don't really know.

1062
00:55:19.862 --> 00:55:23.991
[stammers] I… I accepted the offer.

1063
00:55:24.658 --> 00:55:26.660
and I'm pretty sure
I meant it when I said it.

1064
00:55:28.120 --> 00:55:30.956
But something happened to me
when I walked outta that building.

1065
00:55:31.039 --> 00:55:33.792
[stammers] I-I just thought
that if I took that offer.

1066
00:55:34.376 --> 00:55:37.087
then everything would go right back
to the way it was.

1067
00:55:37.171 --> 00:55:40.924
That I would go right back
to the way I was.

1068
00:55:41.592 --> 00:55:43.760
And you didn't like the way it was?

1069
00:55:43.844 --> 00:55:44.970
I thought I did.

1070
00:55:47.556 --> 00:55:48.807
Turns out I didn't.

1071
00:55:50.058 --> 00:55:54.438
Well. this all sounds very existential.

1072
00:55:56.565 --> 00:55:57.900
I don't know if it's profound

1073
00:55:57.983 --> 00:56:00.569
or you're just swallowing
your own bullshit.

1074
00:56:00.652 --> 00:56:01.653
but either way…

1075
00:56:03.572 --> 00:56:04.573
I want in.

1076
00:56:06.783 --> 00:56:08.118
What? Why?

1077
00:56:09.828 --> 00:56:11.538
'Cause fuck my father-in-law.

1078
00:56:13.373 --> 00:56:15.209
Uh. okay.

1079
00:56:19.087 --> 00:56:21.048
Grace is pregnant. [sighs]

1080
00:56:23.509 --> 00:56:24.760
- Wow.
- Yeah.

1081
00:56:27.387 --> 00:56:29.515
Congratulations.

1082
00:56:36.522 --> 00:56:39.233
Barney getting involved
was a terrible idea.

1083
00:56:39.316 --> 00:56:41.610
But that night.
as we sat in our drenched clothing.

1084
00:56:41.693 --> 00:56:44.154
happily wasted
on a stranger's top-shelf booze.

1085
00:56:44.238 --> 00:56:45.989
watching our friends and neighbors party

1086
00:56:46.073 --> 00:56:48.700
like they were living
in an F. Scott Fitzgerald fever dream.

1087
00:56:49.284 --> 00:56:53.622
For the first time in a while.
the future seemed. well. promising.

1088
00:56:54.164 --> 00:56:56.667
And maybe it was
the painkillers mixing with the booze.

1089
00:56:56.750 --> 00:56:58.836
or maybe it was sheer stupidity.

1090
00:56:58.919 --> 00:57:02.005
but in that moment.
I was just drunk enough to believe it.

1091
00:57:03.215 --> 00:57:04.842
["Burning Down the House" playing]
